{"title":"2018 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Circling the square. Exactly one of these polynomials is a perfect square; that is, can be\nwritten as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/f/2afbe8475414db5aa320daf6df9129cdcb864d0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p(x))^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"19\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/5/2751d79d3bbfb34440d68c685fe6ba7414951749.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> is also a polynomial. Circle the choice that is a perfect square,\nand for that choice, find the square root, the polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/5/2751d79d3bbfb34440d68c685fe6ba7414951749.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>(A) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/2/7a2ad8f5bf3fddaef7809189d72bbab78ede6cb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36-49x^2 + 14x^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"133\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>(B) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/c/87c7f83862f491bca2bc035f38c223c306360814.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36-48x^2 + 14x^4-x^6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"173\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>(C) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/a/b6a4422a62365ffd952f70c72d1392d4f630db46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9-12x + 4x^2 + 12x^3-8x^4 + 4x^6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"264\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>(D) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/9/be94f0c55f00fa29c18a34dfe3eba318f898c220.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36-49x^2 + 15x^4-x^6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"173\" height=\"16\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/9/4a95966962aaf43c27fe9497e9ae130c9d952237.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C; p(x) = 2x^3-2x + 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"179\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNCO_Math_Contest_II\" title=\"2018 UNCO Math Contest II\">2018 UNCO Math Contest II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems\" title=\"2018 UNCO Math Contest II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2018 UNCO Math Contest II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://uncmathcontest.wordpress.com/\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2018 UNCO Math Contest II 